l are infrastructure questions you actively engage with. [high] garrytan (x) — YC president Garry Tan open-sourcing an agent harness his team uses daily — directly in your agent-harness/infra sweet spot and from a high-signal operator. [normal] rahulj51 (x) — Practical dev-tooling pattern for gating agent output quality through a lint step before commit — a workflow guardrail relevant to agent reliability.\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: Claude 5.5 task handling, AI-native roll-ups, agent accountability\n\nabout 12 hours ago\n[high] steipete (x) — Claude 5.5 holds context well enough to drop queued single-tasking; input for agent concurrency design [normal] Isaac Kwemo (linkedin) — AI-native roll-up thesis: frontier founders back deployment over models; Dwelly raised $263M [normal] rahulj51 (x) — IC accountability must shift as agents write most code; org-design angle on the AI coding shift [normal] feross (x) — Composer/Packagist launch sponsorship program with Socket; open-source supply-chain funding model [normal] zeeg (x) — David Cramer pushes trace-first instrumentation; flags agent-assisted tracing tooling as still rough [low] kushxg (x) — Graphite founder on GitHub highlighting the same code-review DX pain points they built for\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: browser WASM tooling, AI infra roll-ups & GPU marketplace\n\nabout 12 hours ago\n[low] michael_chomsky (x) — michael_chomsky (intent) reacting to something significant running in-browser via WebAssembly — suggests a client-side dev tooling or infra breakthrough worth tracking down\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: robotics FM funding, agent identity infra & MCP tooling gaps\n\nabout 11 hours ago\n[high] Liana Karapetyan (linkedin) — GenesisAI raising $500M at $3B shows robotic foundation models now commanding frontier-LLM-lab valuations [high] michael_chomsky (x) — Agent identity verification [normal] dani_avila7 (x) — Concrete infra comparison: org-wide MCP, plugin, and OpenTelemetry support is a real gap where Anthropic leads Codex [normal] zeeg (x) — Sentry's CEO previewing agent-driven incident triage triggered automatically by alerts [normal] theo (x) — OpenAI hitting git scale limits in a single monorepo and upstreaming fixes to git itself [normal] theprimeagen (x) — Sharp prediction that faster, cheaper agents will replace e2e test suites entirely [low] michael_chomsky (x) — Strong opinionated dev tooling comparison favoring documenso over docuseal for document signing\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: DuckDB distribution, native code & agent secrets\n\nabout 10 hours ago\n[normal] Rusty Conover (li) — DuckDB extension distribution gaps, CI build variance [normal] ctatedev (x) — Native SDK code-rendering component, 25 langs, no webviews [normal] matsonj (x) — give agents access to the 1Password CLI for secrets [normal] Max Mikhaylovski (li) — founder geography/burn-rate advantage [low] jhleath (x) — Archil compute now supports SQLite [low] Ali Sozkesen (li) — RoiGuru marketplace ad automation infra [low] mattwensing (x) — startup ideas with highest founder kill rates\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: harness bottlenecks, sandbox architecture, Datadog NRR & AI grants\n\nabout 9 hours ago\n[high] johnkutay (x) — Agent harness is the bottleneck when model upgrades yield zero lift [high] ankrgyl (x) — Separating \"I need a sandbox\" from \"I need a sandbox service\" [normal] Jugal Anchalia (linkedin) — Datadog land-and-expand NRR mechanics (34x cohort expansion) [normal] Atif Shaikh (linkedin) — AI NATION Grant: EUR54K equity-free for Germany AI startups (Aug 9 deadline) [normal] michael_chomsky (x) — Builder humor: localhost:3000 vs vercel.app [normal] rahulj51 (x) — Ontology vs vocabulary terminology in agent design [low] thsottiaux (x) — OpenAI product sprawl through Gmail button creep [low] michael_chomsky (x) — Grafana enthusiasm from a builder\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: agent computer-use & depoliticization trend\n\nabout 8 hours ago\n[normal] mustafaakin (x) — it's a relatable builder-humor vignette of real agent computer-use — Claude orchestrating cross-machine GPU work and proactively flagging a hardware bottleneck [normal] paulg (x) — founder-operator cultural shifts like depoliticization-as-competitive-strategy are the kind of industry-timing observation Burak engages with from builder accounts\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: DESIGN.md for agents, Cloudflare MoQ, token-spend tooling & GPU markets\n\nabout 7 hours ago\n[high] Necati Ozmen (linkedin) — VoltAgent co-founder Necati tracks DESIGN [high] dok2001 (x) — Hard infra/RFW substance on Cloudflare's Media-over-QUIC update: isolated relay provisioning with separate publish/subscribe tokens, filed as an IETF Internet-Draft so other CDNs can interop [normal] yongfook (x) — Sharp, on-taste framing of the buy-vs-build tension AI coding tools create inside eng teams: $200k devs cloning $299/mo SaaS internally instead of shipping product [normal] techguyver (x) — Concrete dev-tooling feature request with a real mechanism: cmux already ships an embedded browser, so URL-hover previews are an offscreen-webview + hover-target away [normal] lumendriada (x) — Points to 'Opus 3 backrooms' as worth a deep-dive for anyone tracking frontier model edge-case behavior — niche but squarely on the model-releases axis of taste [low] raunakdoesdev (x) — Builder-humor signal of serious ML scale: an intern holding 16TB of model weights + data on the training cluster\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: agent UX friction, robotic FMs, OSS agent infra & AI-lab talent flow\n\nabout 6 hours ago\n[high] gdb (x) — OpenAI internal: people reject ChatGPT-bot Slack asks they'd accept from humans [high] Aurora Feng (linkedin) — Cross-embodiment world action models at Neural Motion (liked by Omer Kirnap) [normal] Jacques Nadeau (linkedin) — Now building OSS agent+data infra (Gnarlies) post-Dremio/Arrow [normal] Jad Esber (linkedin) — Amplitude costs ballooned with event volume + auto-renew lock-in [normal] janonacct (x) — Stanford dropout, OpenAI 1st non-tech hire → Anthropic MTS [normal] Seb Johnson (linkedin) — Tapestry VC closed $80M Fund III (Nothing, Fin); Alex Mackenzie endorsed [normal] Enzo Avigo (linkedin) — Ex-June founder → Brand & Content lead at Amplitude (Skates endorsed) [normal] teknium (x) — NVIDIA HQ visit; Jensen signed a Spark dev kit for open-model builders\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: OpenAI Astra math breakthrough, git tooling, stacked-PR obsolescence & AI M&A\n\nabout 5 hours ago\n[high] polynoamial (x) — OpenAI Astra model solved 10 open math/CS problems, frontier reasoning milestone [high] gdb (x) — OpenAI founding team hinting at git tooling; frontier lab moving into dev tools [normal] gergelyorosz (x) — stacked PRs becoming obsolete as AI agents write more code [normal] antirez (x) — running lossless DeepSeek v4 Flash MXFP4 locally at 20+ t/s on 128GB [normal] Saad Saeed (linkedin) — Layla.ai acquired by Expedia Group, AI travel M&A [normal] Sridhar Ramaswamy (linkedin) — Snowflake joining NVIDIA Open Secure AI Alliance [normal] jonathan_gortz (x) — builder humor: 16 Claude Code terminals overnight [low] cagrisarigoz (x) — emotional reality of self-automation\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: OpenRouter provider inconsistency & AI-era bootstrapping thesis\n\nabout 4 hours ago\n[high] antirez (x) — antirez verified locally with MXFP4 greedy continuations that OpenRouter providers for DeepSeek V4 Flash return inconsistent outputs — a concrete infra-trust warning for anyone routing model traffic through aggregators. [normal] Eduardo Mussali (linkedin) — YC W21 founder makes the case that AI decoupled revenue from team size, making bootstrapping structurally viable — directly relevant to founder economics and the small-team competitive advantage.\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: HN AI backlash, LLM dev-tool defaults, Parquet point lookups & Google's missed ChatGPT moment\n\nabout 3 hours ago\n[high] antirez (x) — antirez (Redis creator) highlights sociological resistance to AI-generated results on HN [normal] gorkemcetin (x) — Görkem Çetin (CEO VerifyWise) maps which dev tools LLMs recommend by default [normal] andrewlamb1111 (x) — Andrew Lamb shares Spotify's technique for single-I/O point lookups on Parquet data lakes [normal] _chenglou (x) — chenglou (ReasonML/ReScript creator) recalls Google shelving a pre-ChatGPT internal bot\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: CLI-over-MCP agent wiring, token cheatsheets, repeatable-action frameworks & SF network signals\n\nabout 2 hours ago\n[high] yasser_elsaid_ (x) — CLI-not-MCP pattern for wiring ad/CRM tools into coding agents [high] pidotdev (x) — token-efficiency cheatsheet (/session, /compact) for agent sessions [normal] firatcand (x) — DB-backed framework for repeatable agent actions as yaml plans [normal] mitsuhiko (x) — flags a real shift in AI agents & SOTA models [normal] Matthieu Demolin (linkedin) — Stripe alumni founded both leading AI labs (OpenAI/Anthropic) [normal] sdogruyol (x) — OSS cryload drawing unsolicited contributor PRs [normal] Kaan Eren (linkedin) — names 2 SF people worth following (Amsellem, Valtancoli) [normal] eve_bouff (x) — qm tool turns scattered notes into a daily roadmap\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: Corgi's London café, scaling-velocity thesis, Sim network signal & AI-labor data\n\nabout 1 hour ago\n[normal] Sifted (linkedin) — AI unicorn Corgi opening a 24/7 founder café in Shoreditch [normal] harrystebbings (x) — Sharp VC position that 0→3M ARR speed matters less than 3→20→80M scaling velocity [low] Emir Karabeg (linkedin) — Known contact Emir Karabeg, CEO of AI dev-tool Sim, posting from the company [low] timwonghq (x) — Data point that tech has historically been a small share of job postings, pushing back on AI-blame narratives, plus an Airwallex intern-conversion anecdote.\n\nAGENT\n\nSocial Radar — Aug 1: DeepSeek Flash adoption, Atomarine nuclear DCs, kapa.ai NYC & Claude Code apps\n\n23 minutes ago\n[high] jayair (x) — DeepSeek Flash usage +30%, OpenCode Go subs +30% [normal] Y Combinator (li) — Atomarine: floating nuclear-powered data centers [normal] Emil Sorensen (li) — kapa.ai opens NYC, Hamzah Chaudhary commented [nor",
