Author: Burak Emre Kabakcı <emrekabakci@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 27 18:38:41 2026 +0100

    feat(sidebar): show connected MCP clients in Recent

    A connected MCP client (ChatGPT, Claude Desktop, the CLI) does real work in the
    workspace but had nowhere to appear — its tool calls landed in events and never
    surfaced as anything the user could find.

    Adds an entry per client that deep-links to the events timeline filtered to that
    client's audit trail. It does NOT open a transcript: an MCP tool call has no run
    and no worker, so no transcript exists. The audit trail is the record, and the
    entry points at what actually exists rather than an empty thread.

    Routes like the existing `behavior` entry — listed in Recent, opens elsewhere —
    so this adds one branch beside that precedent instead of a new mechanism. The
    branch sits before the `!isWeb` catch-all, which would otherwise swallow it.

    `clientIds` is a LIST because one client re-registers under the same name (prod
    has 6 ids for "Lobu CLI"), and it round-trips through the URL, the API params,
    and the active-filter check so the drill banner can clear it.

